overview": "Colorado's 4th District leans strongly Republican, and incumbent Lauren Boebert is seeking reelection there. Most professional raters call the race Likely or Solid Republican, though two outlets rate it a Tossup. Prediction markets give Boebert roughly a seven-in-ten chance of holding the seat.\n\nThe race has been shaken in recent weeks by an ethics complaint alleging affairs with staffers and a hush-money payment, which Boebert denies and calls politically motivated. Democrat Eileen Laubacher has dramatically out-raised the incumbent, about $10.3 million to $1.0 million, and holds a large cash advantage heading into the final stretch. No public polls of the general election are available, leaving the true state of the race uncertain. A Libertarian and an independent are also on the ballot.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1824, "margin": -5.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3343, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1945, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2743, "margin": -4.7}]}